files.change:
Add the occurrence stamp. Filename takes the current epoch-milliseconds timestamp per packages/loot-core/migrations/README.md. Exact body, which I ran past the additive-only guard and which passes it:

BEGIN TRANSACTION;
ALTER TABLE transactions ADD COLUMN schedule_occurrence INTEGER DEFAULT NULL;
COMMIT;

The column MUST be INTEGER, not TEXT: date columns are stored as INTEGER yyyymmdd by toDateRepr, and I measured that declaring the stamp TEXT makes AQL's date conversion throw 'fromDateRepr not passed a number'. It must be nullable with default NULL, which the post-cutoff additive-only regime permits and which is what makes the legacy fallback possible. transactions is a synced table and keeps its single id primary key; nothing is dropped or renamed.
